Hilbert polynomial P(n) = 8 n^2 - 8 n + 8 = 8(n^2 - n + 1)
HF = HP for n >= 2
chi(O_V) = P(0) = 8
p_g + q + 1 = chi = 8 (for surface)
If V smooth: p_g = h^2(O_V) = h^0(K_V) = h^0(O_V(1)) = 7
(since K_V = O_V(1) and 7 = dim H^0(P^6, O(1)) restricted)
Irregularity q = 0 (Lefschetz for CI in P^n, n>=3)
Geometric genus p_g = 7

Degenerate curves on V:
V ∩ {a=0}: Pythagorean conic (b^2+c^2=e^2) × sign choices
V ∩ {b=0}, {c=0}: similar
V ∩ {d=0}: a^2+b^2=0 (only over C, no real points except origin)
These give effective divisor classes, suggesting rho(V) > 1
